# =============================================================================
# REQUIRED — three variables. That is the whole list.
# =============================================================================

# ── Public. Compiled into the browser bundle. ────────────────────────────────
# Anything prefixed VITE_ is inlined into the JavaScript every visitor
# downloads, so these are public by definition. On Vercel set them as type
# "Config", not "Secret" — a value the browser receives cannot be a secret, and
# Vercel will refuse the combination.
#
# `vite build` REFUSES to run if either is missing or still a placeholder, so a
# production bundle can never silently ship in demo mode.
#
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key-here

# The anon key is safe to expose: it identifies the project and grants nothing.
# RLS policies are the security boundary.

# ── Private. Server only, never sent to the browser. ─────────────────────────
# Used by /api/booking. On Vercel set it as type "Secret".
# Supabase Dashboard → Project Settings → API → service_role
#
# This key bypasses every RLS policy. It must never carry a VITE_ prefix — if
# it ever does, rotate it immediately, because the build will have published it.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=your-service-role-key-here

# =============================================================================
# RECOMMENDED — not required, but set it before you take real bookings
# =============================================================================

# Salts the SHA-256 of submitter IPs, so rate-limit buckets cannot be reversed
# into a list of addresses. Generate with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# If unset, /api/booking falls back to salting with the service-role key. That
# is still not reversible, but rotating that key resets every rate-limit bucket.
BOOKING_IP_SALT=

# =============================================================================
# NOT NEEDED
# =============================================================================
# There is deliberately no separate SUPABASE_URL. Every project environment
# variable reaches the serverless function as process.env regardless of prefix,
# so /api/booking reads VITE_SUPABASE_URL directly. Maintaining the same URL
# under two names only creates a pair that can drift apart.
#
# It is still honoured if you have it set, so nothing breaks if you leave it.

# =============================================================================
# Local development without a backend
# =============================================================================
# Leave the VITE_ values as placeholders and `npm run dev` falls back to demo
# mode: in-memory fixture data plus a throwaway admin login
# (admin@lumen.dev / admin123). Demo mode is DEV-ONLY — it is compiled out of
# every production build.
